<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		1. Click "IceBlue Compact", then open the daterangebox popup.
		2. In the timebox and in each time input under the calendars, the up and down arrows should fit inside the spin button with space around them.
		Bug: the arrows fill the button, and the up arrow is cut off at the top (compact only).
		3. Click a time input, zoom the browser to 400% and look at the outer edge of the spin button's right corners. It should stay grey.
		Bug: the edge of both corners turns faintly blue while the input has focus (also under "IceBlue"). It is hard to see without zooming.
	</label>
	<hlayout>
		<a id="iceblue" href="?zktheme=iceblue" label="IceBlue"/>
		<a id="iceblue_c" href="?zktheme=iceblue_c" label="IceBlue Compact"/>
		<a id="default" href="?zktheme=default" label="Default"/>
	</hlayout>
	<timebox/>
	<daterangebox showTime="true"/>
</zk>
